In the validation function, use optional chaining and `Array.isArray` when dereferencing properties from potentially missing or malformed input artifacts (such as `fixture` or `fixture.source_selection`) to safely default to an empty array, preventing unhandled `TypeError` exceptions and ensuring the system fails closed gracefully.

```suggestion
  const manifestHasSourceRowsAndPolicyNotes = fixtureList.every((fixture) => {
    const entry = manifestEntryById(manifest, fixture?.fixture_id);
    const sourceArtifactRefs = Array.isArray(entry?.source_artifact_refs) ? entry.source_artifact_refs : [];
    const expectedUiPolicyNotes = Array.isArray(entry?.expected_ui_policy_notes) ? entry.expected_ui_policy_notes : [];
    return entry?.source_row_id === fixture?.source_selection?.source_row_id &&
      sourceArtifactRefs.length > 0 &&
      expectedUiPolicyNotes.length > 0;
  });
```

